{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>A rod.</b> With patach in the qof because it is in construct state." "<b>White almond and plane tree.</b> They are woods; only לַח is the adjective. The Gaon [Saadia] said that לוז is almonds, because it is called thus in the Ishmaelite language, for the two tongues and Aramaic were of one family." "<b>Peeling the white.</b> That peeled the bark, like \"חשף HaShem\" (Isaiah 52:10)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:46:29.031838588Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}